# --- probe/drill policy (explicit, decided 2026-09-28) -------------------
# `apps/web/probe-*.mts` and `apps/web/drill-*.mts` are INTENTIONALLY TRACKED:
# they are the durable honesty-guard smoke suites, liveness probes and
# production-path drills documented in AGENTS.md, and `drill-discord-adapter.mts`
# already sets the precedent. The older `*_probe.ts` / `*probe.ts` patterns
# above do NOT match the `probe-*.mts` naming, so this is recorded here to keep
# the policy deliberate rather than accidental.
# If you write a THROWAWAY script: name it `apps/web/tmp-*.mts` or
# `apps/web/tmp-*.mjs` (both ignored above) instead of `probe-*.mts`, and use a
# run-unique throwaway user (`verify_<name>_${Date.now()}`) whenever it writes to
# user data. The `.mjs` entry was added 2026-09-30: the Gemini Live wire-format
# probes could not use top-level await under tsx, so they were written as `.mjs`,
# and `git add -A` was about to sweep four of them into the commit.
